# playpick cell: mode=clear spec=druid:guardian style=flee size=25
# difficulty=heroic view=390x844,touch save=fresh.
#
# Checked sessions.jsonl first: druid:guardian + flee + mode=clear has one
# prior reading (2026-09-25, 10-normal, 1280x800, fresh) which stalled in
# THE VIGIL at 411.1s, within a couple of units of the wander/good stalls on
# the same cell -- that is direction.md's #6. Nobody has run that same
# spec/style pair through a real 25-heroic evening, and nobody has run a
# *tank* spec under `flee` across a full evening at all: #1's tank-spec
# entries so far are idle (wins clean, repeatedly) and dodge (a protection
# paladin that never taunts cost its 25-heroic raid nine deaths on one pull).
# flee is a third, harder case -- a tank that also runs from every hazard
# rather than merely standing off cooldowns -- and nobody has watched what
# that costs a raid across multiple rooms and multiple pulls rather than one.
#
# A fresh save locks 25-heroic, so #b=marrow&s=25&h=1 unlocks the tier the
# way every other 25-heroic clear/walk script in this ledger does since the
# 2026-09-26 driver-lesson, then backs out to a real RAID -> WALK IN at the
# door rather than the invite's single-fight "visiting" framing.
open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
tap back
tap raid
shot raid-setup
tap next
tap class:druid:guardian
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start
targets
ui
evening flee 260 10
shot end
state
says
bill
